    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0670" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5501: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-08-25T17:00:00-04:00">August 25, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>284. Your 1007, August 25, 4 p.m., paragraph 2. Department approves and suggests
                    consideration of the practicability, in case Colonel Gulick confers with
                    Japanese commandant regarding this or similar questions, of Gulick’s being
                    accompanied by commanding officers of British and perhaps other Legation
                    guards.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
